                <pb facs="0263" n="1223" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1223"/>

                <head>No. 807.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bragg to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 29, 1888</date>.
                        (Received September 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 123.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that, on the
                    26th instant, I received from Consul-General Sutton a letter of Consular-Agent
                    King, inclosing one from the American citizen, B. C. Work, imprisoned in the
                    State of Tamaulipas, on charge of homicide, copy of which letter and its
                    inclosure are made inclosures herewith.</p>
                <p>Upon receipt of such communication I addressed Mr. Mariscal a note, copy whereof
                    is also herewish inclosed, which I trust will meet your approval.</p>
                <p>This case will be recalled by reference to my Nos. 10 and 35.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwd. S. Bragg.</hi></signed></closer>





